@startuml
skinparam backgroundColor #FFFFFF
skinparam defaultFontColor #000000
skinparam shadowing false
skinparam ArrowColor #000000
skinparam ComponentBorderColor #000000
skinparam ComponentFontColor #000000
skinparam RectangleBorderColor #000000
skinparam RectangleFontColor #000000
skinparam DatabaseBorderColor #000000
skinparam DatabaseFontColor #000000

title Product Management Flow After Autonomous Engine

actor "LLM / Agent" as Agent #E8F0FE
component "MCP Server\nTool Router" as Server #D9EAD3
component "Product Management Engine\nanalysis + governance" as Engine #D0E0FF
component "Inventory Collectors\nLinear issues/cycles + GitHub issues" as Inventory #FFF4CC
component "Work Normalizer\nsingle backlog model" as Normalizer #EADCF8
component "Policy Scorer\nstale + next-cycle ranking" as Scorer #D9EAD3
component "Signal Vetting Gate\nevidence + confidence checks" as Vetting #FCE5CD
component "Template Enforcer\nproduct opportunity bodies" as Template #FFF4CC
component "Linear Template Service" as LinearWrapper #D0E0FF
component "GitHub App Service" as GitHubWrapper #FCE5CD
database "Linear API\nissues + cycles" as LinearApi #EAF7EA
database "GitHub REST API\nissues + PRs" as GitHubApi #FFE5E5

Agent --> Server : product_engine_analyze_backlog
Server --> Engine : run planning analysis
Engine --> Inventory : collect live work
Inventory --> LinearWrapper : list issues + cycles
Inventory --> GitHubWrapper : list repository issues
LinearWrapper --> LinearApi : team inventory
GitHubWrapper --> GitHubApi : repository inventory
Inventory --> Normalizer : source snapshots
Normalizer --> Scorer : normalized work items
Scorer --> Engine : stale items,\nprevious-cycle carry-over,\nnext-cycle candidates
Engine --> Agent : governed planning report

Agent --> Server : product_engine_create_proactive_issues
Server --> Engine : vet product signals
Engine --> Vetting : require evidence,\nimpact/recommendation,\nconfidence threshold
Vetting --> Template : build opportunity body
Template --> LinearWrapper : create Linear issue
Template --> GitHubWrapper : create GitHub issue

note bottom of Engine #F3F3F3
The MCP server now owns product governance:
it can inspect work, flag stale items,
rank next-cycle candidates, and create
new issues only after signal vetting.
end note

@enduml
